      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s post office opened in 1854, just a year after the town was founded.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etna_Green%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Etna Green Elevator, built in 1907, still operates today and is a rare surviving grain elevator.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitkosciuskocounty.org/explore/communities/etna-green/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Etna Green Museum in Heritage Park preserves the town’s history and showcases artifacts from early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitkosciuskocounty.org/explore/communities/etna-green/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Original settlers included Robert Reid, Solomon Klingerman and Charles Rockhill, who arrived in 1843.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.inkfreenews.com/2025/06/30/timeline-from-the-past-etna-green-turkey-creek-history/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Etna Green takes its name from Etna Township, reflecting the area’s early administrative organization.",
